00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:04.860
- You, Dead Eye?

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:05.860
- Yep.

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:06.870
- Draw!

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.210
- Mama!

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:19.310
- Keep on the hot sun.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:23.860
- One boy got St. Vitus and he just won't give up.

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:25.860
Look at him.

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:27.860
- Well, so long, Dead Eye.

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:28.860
- So long, Sheriff.

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:30.000
- I just...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.200
Oh, did I?

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:35.590
Yes, wish they'd let me--

00:22:35.590 --> 00:22:37.110
Oh.

00:22:37.110 --> 00:22:38.200
Hello.

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:58.000
Me, how are they ever going to say this is a live show?

00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.380
Hello, dead-eye.

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:00.000
Give me the--

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:02.760
You've got to take me back, Emmylou.

00:23:02.760 --> 00:23:04.340
I'm through with gunfighting.

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:05.860
I've given up everything.

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:07.000
You'll never change.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.400
You've got blood on your hands.

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.780
No, that ain't blood.

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.080
That's whiskey smell.

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:12.780
You'll buy.

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:14.220
Emmylou, don't leave me.

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:15.720
Look, I'm giving up my guns.

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:16.820
I won't fight anymore.

00:23:16.820 --> 00:23:17.600
I'm done with it.

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:18.620
I'm through killing.

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:20.420
You've got to take me back, Emmylou.

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.520
If you promise never to kill anybody again.

00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:23.930
I promise.

00:23:23.930 --> 00:23:25.550
You'll never shoot anybody again, no matter what?

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:28.260
Never reach for a gun as long as I live.

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:30.000
OK, drawn.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:36.400
Look what you've done.

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:39.480
The only thing that mattered in the world to me.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:41.080
Look what you've done.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:43.100
My favorite bartender.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:45.720
Thank you.

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:02.210
Thank you very much, partners.

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:06.700
I am now going down to the old corral.

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:11.220
It's really a new corral, but we never referred anything into the West as old.

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:12.000
I mean, new.

00:24:12.580 --> 00:24:17.490
So I'm going down to the old corral and take my old saddle, which is a new saddle,

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:19.800
and I'm going to throw it on old paint.

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:21.440
That's my wife.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.190
She's really old.

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:27.630
She could use paint, too.

00:24:28.630 --> 00:24:30.000
Well, thanks for our little visit.

00:24:30.090 --> 00:24:37.720
behalf of Geritol. So until we meet again, partners, adios amigo, which in English means

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:39.000
"Hasta la vista."

00:25:24.760 --> 00:25:29.960
with Grant Skelton brought to you by the remarkable new tonic that helps you feel strongly fast.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:37.420
The Red Skelton Show originated live from the television city in Hollywood and is a CBS Television Network production.
